# Reviewed divergences between the pinned oracle and ztsc.
#
# `.expected` snapshots are pure oracle output and are never hand-edited, so
# `node test/conformance/gen_expected.js test/conformance --check` is a real
# gate. Every deliberate difference is recorded here instead, one per line:
#
#   <case-path>  -TS<code> [<file>] <line>   oracle reports it, ztsc does not
#   <case-path>  +TS<code> [<file>] <line>   ztsc reports it, the oracle does not
#
# (`<file>` only for directory cases, matching the snapshot format.)
#
# Policy: a missed error (`-`) is acceptable when it is deterministic and
# reasoned; a false positive is not. A `+` entry therefore needs a stronger
# justification than a `-` entry and is only defensible when the same
# diagnostic is also present in the snapshot at a different span.
#
# The registry is self-cleaning: run_conformance.zig fails the case if an entry
# stops describing reality (ztsc started emitting a `-` line, stopped emitting
# a `+` line, the oracle dropped a `-` line, or the case is gone). It cannot be
# used to hide a regression.

# TS2417 (class static side incorrectly extends base static side) is not
# implemented: ztsc does not relate `typeof Derived` to `typeof Base` when a
# derived static shadows a base static incompatibly. Under-report of a whole
# check, not a span/precision difference.
classes/033_static_inherit.ts  -TS2417 14

# TS2589 at the structural-relation recursion cap. ztsc's cap assumes the
# relation and stays silent rather than reporting at the cap, because reporting
# there would false-positive genuinely-valid deep recursive types the oracle
# accepts (real form-library `PathValue` shapes). Deliberate, deterministic
# under-report; the cases exist to prove these inputs keep checking without
# stack-overflowing. See the comment in each case file.
instantiation/003_recursive_alias_relation_cap.ts  -TS2589 19
instantiation/010_growing_bareref_no_eager_expand.ts  -TS2589 12

# Same diagnostic, different anchor: the oracle reports TS2589 at the deep
# template node inside the alias declaration (line 16); ztsc reports it at the
# annotation that triggered the instantiation (line 18). The error IS produced
# and the TS2322 on line 18 matches — this is a report-SITE divergence on one
# diagnostic, hand-verified, not an extra error.
instantiation/018_growing_template_hole_no_loop.ts  -TS2589 16
instantiation/018_growing_template_hole_no_loop.ts  +TS2589 18

# An `exports`-map subpath that the map does not name is routed to an opaque
# `any` module rather than left dangling. Dangling the specifier was not
# crash-safe under parallel resolution (it dangled a symbol -> SIGABRT), so the
# TS2307 the oracle emits is deliberately traded for crash safety. See the
# comment in the case entry.ts.
modules/39_exports_subpath_block  -TS2307 entry.ts 12

# A compound assignment (`x += 1`, `x -= 1`, ...) does not check that its
# result is assignable back to the target, so the oracle's TS2322 on
# `mv += 1` where `mv: number & { _brand }` is missed. Pre-existing and
# independent of the operand classification the case is about: the plain
# assignments on lines 11-12 of the same case prove `number` is still not
# assignable to the brand. Deterministic under-report of a whole check.
operators/004_branded_intersection_not_numeric.ts  -TS2322 31
